Till you want some more</i>


00:00:39.921 --> 00:00:43.652
<i>'Cause all I see is an open door</i>


00:00:43.825 --> 00:00:47.625
<i>And I see where it's leading me
All of this energy</i>


00:00:47.795 --> 00:00:51.390
<i>Been bottled up way too long
It's powerful, powerful</i>


00:00:51.566 --> 00:00:55.127
<i>You see what I'm getting at
I'm ready for all of that</i>


00:00:55.303 --> 00:00:58.830
<i>If I'm not a star, you're blind</i>


00:00:59.007 --> 00:01:02.374
<i>I've got rings on my fingers
And glitter in my hair</i>


00:01:02.544 --> 00:01:05.809
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:09.677
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:09.851 --> 00:01:13.878
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:14.055 --> 00:01:17.650
<i>I've got high heel stilettos
And I'm kicking in doors</i>


00:01:17.825 --> 00:01:20.953
<i>And kissing your ass
Ain't what my lipstick's for</i>


00:01:21.129 --> 00:01:24.895
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:25.066 --> 00:01:28.058
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:28.236 --> 00:01:31.728
Where's breakfast?
I want waffles, spaghetti!


00:01:31.906 --> 00:01:35.171
Spaghetti waffles! Whoo. Whoo!


00:01:35.343 --> 00:01:37.368
Victor. Victor.
Please wait in the house, please.


00:01:38.813 --> 00:01:41.646
My body is entering hunger shock.


00:01:43.017 --> 00:01:46.714
Oh, bad news.
The cat pooped in the den.


00:01:46.888 --> 00:01:50.187
Worse news, I used your blanket
to clean it up.


00:01:50.358 --> 00:01:52.292
- We don't have a cat.
- No kidding.


00:02:27.395 --> 00:02:30.956
Oh. L... Sorry.
I didn't think you'd be awake.


00:02:31.132 --> 00:02:32.292
You have an appointment...


00:02:32.467 --> 00:02:35.061
...with Guy Morgan,
I didn't think you'd wanna be late.


00:02:35.236 --> 00:02:38.171
Oh, look at you thinking. Cute.


00:02:38.339 --> 00:02:40.398
But I always have time for my portrait.


00:02:40.575 --> 00:02:42.099
Look alive. Paint.


00:02:42.543 --> 00:02:44.374
I'm feeling spiritually blocked.


00:02:44.545 --> 00:02:46.376
Draw me a sesame seed bath.


00:02:46.814 --> 00:02:47.940
Bath. Now.


00:02:48.916 --> 00:02:50.781
Now, make momma look more beautiful
and thinner.


00:02:52.153 --> 00:02:53.381
And make that water more quiet.


00:02:56.958 --> 00:02:59.051
- Bev, you awake?
- Of course I'm awake.


00:02:59.227 --> 00:03:01.821
If I waited for you, I'd never be on time.


00:03:01.996 --> 00:03:04.430
Lucky you never wait for me then.


00:03:17.912 --> 00:03:19.345
Victor, no.


00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:27.954
Uh, don't you want a glass?


00:03:28.122 --> 00:03:34.118
Hmm. Earthy. A tad fishy.
Lovely gravel finish.


00:03:34.595 --> 00:03:37.120
Did you let Victor put worms
in the blender again?


00:03:37.832 --> 00:03:39.527
Yes. I mean, no.


00:03:41.035 --> 00:03:42.627
I mean, it just happened.


00:03:43.171 --> 00:03:44.536
You know nothing can kill me.


00:03:45.707 --> 00:03:47.334
Nothing.


00:03:51.979 --> 00:03:54.846
Step on it, Katie.
I cannot be late for this meeting.


00:03:55.016 --> 00:03:56.381
Just run them over if you have to.


00:03:59.187 --> 00:04:02.213
Hello? No, the kids don't need a library.


00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:05.621
I am the dean, and the dean gets
what she wants, and I wanna remodel.


00:04:05.793 --> 00:04:09.251
You're just boring. I'm being honest.
I don't know what else to tell you.


00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:12.524
And I wanted my office done
for my meeting with Guy Morgan...


00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:14.361
...the music mogul, but no.


00:04:14.535 --> 00:04:16.730
And using Bollywood
as a theme for the dance?


00:04:16.904 --> 00:04:20.362
That's totally un-American.
I don't care if it was my idea.


00:04:22.043 --> 00:04:24.307
Hello.
Oh. Oh.


00:04:24.479 --> 00:04:27.175
I'm Dean Van Ravensway,
and you must be...


00:04:27.348 --> 00:04:30.442
- Guy Morgan.
- Ah, yes. Guy Morgan, a pleasure.


00:04:30.618 --> 00:04:32.108
You look like a man who knows things.


00:04:32.286 --> 00:04:34.846
Aha, even some things I shouldn't know.


00:04:35.022 --> 00:04:36.819
- And I'm Luke.
Great.


00:04:50.371 --> 00:04:54.330
<i>So tell me, Guy, is it true?
Are you the new judge on Idol?</i>


00:04:54.509 --> 00:04:57.876
Well, let's just say
that Randy may be in the doghouse.


00:04:58.045 --> 00:04:59.910
- Now, let's talk about my son.
- Of course.


00:05:00.081 --> 00:05:02.515
- Have you reviewed your schedule, Luke?
- Yes, I have.


00:05:02.683 --> 00:05:06.210
In fact, um, I'd like to add a music class.
Um, the music theory...


00:05:06.387 --> 00:05:09.948
Wellesley has a great business program.
That's why we're here.


00:05:10.458 --> 00:05:15.361
There are two types of people
in the music biz: Artists and businessmen.


00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:17.361
- Luke is a businessman.
- Of course.


00:05:17.865 --> 00:05:21.858
Katie, get in here. Look alive.
Make yourself useful.


00:05:25.339 --> 00:05:27.671
Luke is gonna need a tour of the campus.


00:05:28.142 --> 00:05:33.205
So text Bev and ask her
to escort Mr. Morgan around campus.


00:05:33.514 --> 00:05:36.642
Now, Luke, if you are half as talented
a producer as your father...


00:05:36.818 --> 00:05:39.878
The verdict's still out.
He hasn't earned it.


00:05:41.556 --> 00:05:43.820
Heard the story of how I started
in the music business?


00:05:43.991 --> 00:05:47.427
- Yes, everybody's heard it, Dad.
- Then everybody should know how it goes.


00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:51.924
There I was,
working for The Rolling Stones...


00:05:52.099 --> 00:05:53.930
...when Mick himself...
- Dad.


00:05:55.203 --> 00:05:58.400
Fine. As I said,
the verdict is still out on my son.


00:05:58.573 --> 00:06:02.339
He just produced an album
with the Fruity Dangers?


00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:04.171
Do you mean Danger Fruit?


00:06:05.346 --> 00:06:07.109
That record was amazing.


00:06:07.281 --> 00:06:10.250
I forgot what they were called because
they made me absolutely no money.


00:06:11.752 --> 00:06:14.220
Thank you. Rare I meet anyone
who's heard their album.


00:06:14.388 --> 00:06:17.289
What, are you kidding?
They're a cult phenomenon.


00:06:17.458 --> 00:06:19.119
I'm sorry. Why are you talking?


00:06:20.661 --> 00:06:26.224
What I need is for Luke to learn
to spot a commercially viable star.


00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.561
Image drives the bottom line, right?


00:06:28.736 --> 00:06:32.103
I feel you. Would we have Bieber Fever
if he were an ugly troll?


00:06:32.273 --> 00:06:34.434
Actually, he is a tad hobbit-like, isn't he?


00:06:34.609 --> 00:06:36.975
I'd like Luke
to produce your Semester Showcase...


00:06:37.144 --> 00:06:41.046
...to see if he can identify sellable talent.
- I produce the Semester Showcase.


00:06:42.183 --> 00:06:44.276
I will double your Showcase budget.


00:06:44.785 --> 00:06:47.151
I will invite every talent scout I know.


00:06:47.722 --> 00:06:49.849
This could be the beginning
of a relationship...


00:06:50.024 --> 00:06:51.992
...between Wellesley
and Kensington Records.


00:06:52.159 --> 00:06:54.150
Looks like we have a new producer.


00:06:54.328 --> 00:06:57.297
Oh, and this is my daughter, Bev.


00:06:57.732 --> 00:07:00.496
Bev, this is the platinum-selling,
Grammy-winning...


00:07:00.668 --> 00:07:03.569
...and very handsome producer,
Guy Morgan.


00:07:03.738 --> 00:07:05.569
Could you give his son, Luke, a tour?


00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:08.607
Sure. Would you like
to see the Wellesley perks?


00:07:08.776 --> 00:07:11.404
Um, yes, brilliant. Sure.


00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:13.870
- Katie.
I love your accent.


00:07:14.048 --> 00:07:15.640
Katie.
Wanna come over tonight?


00:07:15.816 --> 00:07:18.182
What are you still doing here? Go.


00:07:18.352 --> 00:07:21.753
Guy and I have things we need to discuss.
Out. Now.


00:07:22.356 --> 00:07:27.760
So, Guy, you've gotta tell me,
what was that like working under Mick?


00:07:36.637 --> 00:07:38.332
Watch out.


00:07:38.806 --> 00:07:40.831
- Dangerous balls.
- Ha, ha. Thanks.


00:07:41.842 --> 00:07:45.437
- So you womanned up and did it?
Hey!


00:07:45.613 --> 00:07:47.410
- Oh, I did it.
Hey!


00:07:47.581 --> 00:07:49.947
- What happened?
Can we have our ball?


00:07:50.117 --> 00:07:51.482
I didn't give my CD to Luke.


00:07:51.652 --> 00:07:54.644
I snuck it in his dad's bag.


00:07:54.822 --> 00:07:58.781
But Guy Morgan has your demo.
That's huge. What you need is a champion.


00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:00.689
No, what I need is to graduate.


00:08:01.529 --> 00:08:03.429
You giving our ball back or what?


00:08:03.597 --> 00:08:07.226
Oh, do you want this?


00:08:12.039 --> 00:08:15.304
She shoots, she scores.
Unlike you, soccer boy.


00:08:17.645 --> 00:08:21.376
Oh, so spill it. Is Luke Morgan
as hot as everyone Tweets he is?


00:08:21.549 --> 00:08:22.914
Hotter.


00:08:23.084 --> 00:08:24.711
You should ask him to the dance.


00:08:24.885 --> 00:08:27.115
Because I'm so forward with guys.


00:08:27.288 --> 00:08:29.848
First time for everything, right?


00:08:36.998 --> 00:08:38.693
- Hi, Luke.
- Hello.


00:08:38.866 --> 00:08:40.094
You have to hear my demo.


00:08:40.568 --> 00:08:43.628
It's a retro-funk-jazz explosion.


00:08:43.804 --> 00:08:45.999
Back off. I was here first.


00:08:46.173 --> 00:08:49.631
Hold on, hold up. Please hold on.
My boy does not want your demos yet.


00:08:49.810 --> 00:08:52.074
Walk away. Move along. Bye.


00:08:52.246 --> 00:08:55.613
It was nice chatting
or whatever that was.


00:08:55.883 --> 00:08:58.215
- Yes, hi, I'm, uh...
- Luke Morgan, right?


00:08:58.386 --> 00:08:59.910
Who is producing the Showcase.


00:09:00.087 --> 00:09:02.988
I don't think I'm gonna do the Showcase,
so I need to keep a low profile...


00:09:03.157 --> 00:09:06.593
Yeah, yeah. Listen close now.
There's two kinds of people in this school.


00:09:06.761 --> 00:09:10.288
There are the wannabes
and there's gonnabes.


00:09:10.464 --> 00:09:15.629
You and I, we're gonnabes. What do we do?
We stay away from the wannabes, all right?


00:09:15.803 --> 00:09:19.364
And girls named Yolanda. There are three
of them and they are certifiably...


00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:21.633
Crazy? You attract
crazy women? Shocking.


00:09:21.809 --> 00:09:24.710
It may seem like I don't have game,
but ladies love a listener.


00:09:24.879 --> 00:09:27.006
Plus, I'm telling you,
let me help you find acts.


00:09:27.181 --> 00:09:30.207
- Ah, so you're a talent scout?
- Well, bottom line, I'm a DJ.


00:09:30.384 --> 00:09:32.579
- Oh, you're a DJ as well?
- Check this.


00:09:41.128 --> 00:09:42.390
Whoa.


00:09:42.563 --> 00:09:45.657
Okay, yes. You could be very useful.
It was nice meeting you.


00:09:45.833 --> 00:09:48.495
You got a girl for the dance?
Because I can hook you up.


00:09:48.669 --> 00:09:49.829
Uh, no. Thanks.


00:09:50.004 --> 00:09:53.405
Uh, but what do you know
about Bev Van Ravensway?


00:09:53.574 --> 00:09:55.235
- Supposed to see her tonight.
- Bev?


00:09:55.409 --> 00:09:56.433
- Yeah.
- She's hot...


00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:59.078
...but the girl
is mad, mad drama, okay?


00:09:59.246 --> 00:10:01.646
I am talking to you
and you don't even know my name.


00:10:01.816 --> 00:10:03.716
- I'm Mickey O'Malley.
- Mickey O'Malley.


00:10:03.884 --> 00:10:05.511
A rarity in the Irish community.


00:10:06.087 --> 00:10:08.180
Om.


00:10:08.989 --> 00:10:11.617
RAVl: Om.
- Om.


00:10:11.792 --> 00:10:13.885
- Om.
- Om!


00:10:14.061 --> 00:10:16.586
This is not a contest, Ms. Gail.


00:10:16.964 --> 00:10:18.591
Just concentrate on your breathing.


00:10:20.101 --> 00:10:21.261
My butt is numb.


00:10:21.602 --> 00:10:24.799
If your butt is suffering,
then you are suffering.


00:10:24.972 --> 00:10:28.430
In fact, your entire life is suffering. Why?


00:10:28.609 --> 00:10:31.703
Because you crave
that which is meaningless.


00:10:31.879 --> 00:10:33.870
Are you calling me shallow?


00:10:34.949 --> 00:10:40.785
No, I'm saying to stop your craving
and release your butt.


00:10:40.955 --> 00:10:44.516
Just release it. Release it, yeah.
Release that butt.


00:10:45.392 --> 00:10:48.452
<i>Release that butt
Oh, yeah, release that butt</i>


00:10:48.629 --> 00:10:51.223
<i>Oh, yeah, release that butt</i>


00:10:51.398 --> 00:10:52.695
Mrs. Van Ravensway?


00:10:52.867 --> 00:10:55.392
What part
of "if you interrupt my meditation...


00:10:55.569 --> 00:10:58.766
...I will jerk your tail in a knot"
do you not understand?


00:10:58.939 --> 00:11:01.373
You told me
to tell you when dinner was ready.


00:11:01.542 --> 00:11:04.943
Oh, thank God.
I'm craving some bourbon.


00:11:08.716 --> 00:11:10.183
Victor.


00:11:10.351 --> 00:11:15.584
- Oh. Um, dinner's ready.
- Tell me something I don't know.


00:11:39.246 --> 00:11:43.683
Do you have any idea how stressful it is
to run this academy?


00:11:44.018 --> 00:11:46.509
Yes, I spent the money at the spa.


00:11:47.555 --> 00:11:50.217
<i>Five thousand dollars a night
is not very expensive...</i>


00:11:50.391 --> 00:11:54.953
<i>... when you think about the alternative,
which is me having a nervous breakdown.</i>


00:11:58.265 --> 00:11:59.289
<i>Ow.</i>


00:11:59.466 --> 00:12:01.900
<i>What are you doing?
I'm on the phone.</i>


00:12:02.069 --> 00:12:03.661
<i>- I'm cleansing.
Heh, heh.</i>


00:12:03.871 --> 00:12:06.101
Mac and cheese.


00:12:07.007 --> 00:12:10.135
<i>I don't need your spiritual counseling.</i>


00:12:10.678 --> 00:12:12.236
<i>I'm thinking of firing you.</i>


00:12:17.751 --> 00:12:21.118
Pace yourself, Ms. Gail,
or you will not be one with everything.


00:12:21.288 --> 00:12:24.621
Honey, that's what I got you for.
Now, make me one with everything.


00:12:26.026 --> 00:12:29.223
This Showcase is giving me the vapors.


00:12:29.396 --> 00:12:31.489
How did this become my life?


00:12:31.665 --> 00:12:34.657
Did I ever tell you all about the time
I nearly got my big break?


00:12:34.835 --> 00:12:36.325
Yes.
- Good.


00:12:36.503 --> 00:12:37.936
Then you all know how it goes.


00:12:38.372 --> 00:12:40.567
<i>I ain't gonna leap, I'm gonna jump</i>


00:12:40.741 --> 00:12:43.073
<i>Find my way right out of this dump</i>


00:12:45.913 --> 00:12:48.780
- I had talent, and they made me...
A laughingstock.


00:12:50.551 --> 00:12:51.848
Now look at me.


00:12:52.019 --> 00:12:54.510
I got two ungrateful kids...


00:12:54.688 --> 00:12:57.680
...a dwarfish, hairy, elfin servant...


00:12:57.858 --> 00:12:59.849
...and a random
tablecloth-wearing Asian...


00:13:00.027 --> 00:13:02.257
- Indian.
- Who makes no sense at all, ever.


00:13:02.429 --> 00:13:04.192
Why don't you have another drink, Mom.


00:13:05.733 --> 00:13:07.928
Katie, napkin me.


00:13:08.102 --> 00:13:10.593
I have got to impress Guy Morgan...


00:13:11.005 --> 00:13:14.236
...so I can stop pretending to care
about this insufferable school...


00:13:14.408 --> 00:13:18.174
...and we can all move to Hollywood where
no one pretends to care about anything.


00:13:18.345 --> 00:13:21.974
Mom, I think that you're forgetting
about the most important thing. Me.


00:13:22.916 --> 00:13:25.316
Guy will give me a deal
as soon as he hears me sing.


00:13:25.486 --> 00:13:28.080
- I doubt that.
- No, I've been practicing really hard.


00:13:28.255 --> 00:13:31.122
My voice teacher says
I've transcended to a whole new level.


00:13:31.292 --> 00:13:32.316
Yeah, I doubt it.


00:13:32.493 --> 00:13:35.053
When my first single drops,
I'll buy you that mansion...


00:13:35.229 --> 00:13:37.163
...in the Hollywood Hills...


00:13:37.331 --> 00:13:40.357
...and you can finally afford
to have your legs lengthened.


00:13:40.534 --> 00:13:42.559
- Oh, ba...
- Ms. Gail.


00:13:42.736 --> 00:13:44.704
- Miss Bev has clarity.
Katie.


00:13:44.872 --> 00:13:45.896
- You see...
- Look.


00:13:46.073 --> 00:13:49.941
- The lowly peasant tills the soil
for 40 years without any rain.


00:13:50.110 --> 00:13:53.511
But the unemployed salesman
who has recently discovered hydroponics...


00:13:53.681 --> 00:13:56.775
...all of a sudden gets disgusted by the...
- And see? No sense.


00:13:56.950 --> 00:13:59.248
- That didn't make any sense.
- Let me finish. You...


00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:01.354
Oh, I doubt it. You have me pray all day.


00:14:01.522 --> 00:14:03.752
- I don't feel nothing.
- You don't have a soul.


00:14:03.924 --> 00:14:07.121
No, you don't have soul.
- I have a many souls. I'll give you one.


00:14:07.294 --> 00:14:11.560
- Where's your third eye? Turn that thing on.
- I have a fourth eye too. You wanna see it?


00:14:11.732 --> 00:14:13.700
- What?
- Shh.


00:14:14.201 --> 00:14:17.728
I wanna be 6'4". Wow me, Bev.


00:14:20.274 --> 00:14:25.712
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:25.879 --> 00:14:28.439
Just stop. Stop the wowing, okay?


00:14:28.615 --> 00:14:30.708
What's wrong?
- Somehow you've gotten worse.


00:14:30.884 --> 00:14:32.613
I don't know how that was possible...


00:14:32.786 --> 00:14:35.414
...but there isn't enough Auto-Tune
that's gonna fix you.


00:14:35.589 --> 00:14:38.922
- Well, Katie's bad playing threw me off.
- I don't think it was that.


00:14:39.093 --> 00:14:40.720
Again.


00:14:40.894 --> 00:14:42.452
Really? Okay.


00:14:42.629 --> 00:14:48.261
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:48.435 --> 00:14:49.561
Ouch.


00:14:49.737 --> 00:14:52.797
I could belch the song better.


00:14:54.408 --> 00:14:56.569
Have you been drinking
the floor wax again?


00:14:56.744 --> 00:14:58.211
Anything to forget I live here.


00:14:58.379 --> 00:15:01.280
Ugh. My head is buzzing
like a skeeter on a septic tank.


00:15:01.448 --> 00:15:05.350
- Ravi, meditate me.
Good luck, buddy.


00:15:05.719 --> 00:15:09.382
Well, it doesn't matter,
because I have my own plan.


00:15:13.594 --> 00:15:15.960
Does it make me a bad person
that I kind of enjoyed that?


00:15:16.130 --> 00:15:17.859
No.


00:15:18.031 --> 00:15:20.329
Hmm. Nice work.


00:15:32.513 --> 00:15:35.812
- Guess who's on his way over.
- Not now, Victor, I'm busy.


00:15:35.983 --> 00:15:38.451
Guess or prepare to get creamed.


00:15:48.929 --> 00:15:52.023
Victor! Victor! Victor, stop!


00:15:56.904 --> 00:15:58.633
<i>I've got rings on my fingers</i>


00:15:58.806 --> 00:15:59.898
<i>And glitter in my hair</i>


00:16:00.073 --> 00:16:04.169
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:16:04.344 --> 00:16:05.675
<i>I'm gonna run...</i>


00:16:05.846 --> 00:16:08.610
- Ha-ha-ha.
- Victor, what are you doing?


00:16:09.049 --> 00:16:10.346
Victor!


00:16:10.517 --> 00:16:13.748
Victor, where did you put my clothes?


00:16:13.921 --> 00:16:16.082
- Surprise!
- What? No.


00:16:19.593 --> 00:16:21.220
I'm gonna kill you. Victor!


00:16:31.138 --> 00:16:32.298
Oh, hi, Katie.


00:16:32.473 --> 00:16:33.872
You are evil. Let me in.


00:16:34.041 --> 00:16:37.477
I control every lock on this property.


00:16:37.644 --> 00:16:39.305
Crap.


00:16:42.716 --> 00:16:44.411
This is insane.


00:16:44.585 --> 00:16:48.646
Yeah, try the shed, it's unlocked, idiot.


00:16:58.432 --> 00:17:00.525
You gotta be kidding me.


00:17:02.269 --> 00:17:03.896
Crap.


00:17:07.207 --> 00:17:10.802
How did such an untalented daughter
spring from my loins?


00:17:10.978 --> 00:17:14.778
Focus, Ms. Gail. We are making
an offering to your personal deity.


00:17:14.948 --> 00:17:17.075
Tell him to give me fame and fortune.


00:17:17.251 --> 00:17:18.946
Not exactly how it works.


00:17:19.119 --> 00:17:21.679
<i>Now, breathe through your Mula Bandha.</i>


00:17:21.855 --> 00:17:24.915
Oh, honey, if I could do that,
I'd get a million hits on YouTube.


00:17:25.092 --> 00:17:27.322
How much longer is this gonna take?
Ugh.


00:17:27.494 --> 00:17:29.621
The prayer or the fame and fortune?


00:17:31.965 --> 00:17:33.432
Ha, ha. See you later.


00:17:39.606 --> 00:17:41.471
Victor.


00:17:45.312 --> 00:17:46.745
Katie?


00:17:47.948 --> 00:17:50.178
- Luke.
- Katie.


00:17:50.384 --> 00:17:53.649
- Are you wearing a doormat?
- Yes.


00:17:53.820 --> 00:17:56.584
- Welcome.
- Why, thank you.


00:17:57.624 --> 00:17:59.455
The truth. Um...


00:18:00.761 --> 00:18:04.094
My stepbrother locked me
outside of the house.


00:18:04.264 --> 00:18:05.595
Naked.


00:18:06.633 --> 00:18:08.931
Oh, sorry. You should...
You should take my jacket.


00:18:09.102 --> 00:18:10.626
Oh.
- Oh, no, no.


00:18:13.073 --> 00:18:14.165
There.


00:18:14.341 --> 00:18:17.538
- Thanks. Now the pants.
- Hmm?


00:18:22.149 --> 00:18:23.776
I'm kidding.


00:18:24.318 --> 00:18:26.149
- You got me.
- Ha, ha.


00:18:26.486 --> 00:18:27.510
No, no.


00:18:27.688 --> 00:18:31.089
One more parent-teacher conference,
I swear I'm gonna lose it.


00:18:31.258 --> 00:18:33.453
Look at me. I'm an educator.


00:18:34.061 --> 00:18:38.725
I have no real skills. And I will die
before I go back to my daddy's farm.


00:18:39.232 --> 00:18:43.032
You tell my personal deity
to help me achieve Guy Morgan. Do it.


00:18:43.203 --> 00:18:45.797
I'll put another banana on the altar.


00:18:49.676 --> 00:18:51.337
What is that?


00:18:51.912 --> 00:18:54.176
Do you hear angels singing?


00:18:54.348 --> 00:18:56.316
Perhaps the gods
have answered your prayer.


00:18:57.517 --> 00:18:59.246
Hey. What...?


00:19:12.099 --> 00:19:14.590
<i>- This is Gail Van Ravensway.
Hello.</i>


00:19:14.768 --> 00:19:16.395
Guy Morgan here. How are you?


00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:18.697
Oh, well, hello, Guy.


00:19:18.872 --> 00:19:21.136
What a surprise
to see you calling this number.


00:19:21.308 --> 00:19:22.332
Do you hear this?


00:19:22.509 --> 00:19:24.170
<i>I can justify</i>


00:19:24.344 --> 00:19:26.039
That's the demo your girl, Katie...


00:19:26.213 --> 00:19:28.545
<i>... slipped into my briefcase.</i>


00:19:28.715 --> 00:19:30.910
And it sounds like money, dear.


00:19:31.084 --> 00:19:32.949
She gave you a CD?


00:19:33.120 --> 00:19:36.487
Oh, well. Well, ain't that the berries.


00:19:37.724 --> 00:19:41.592
Ravi, what frigging god did you pray to?


00:19:42.829 --> 00:19:46.925
Guy, yeah, it seems someone's
not being entirely honest here.


00:19:48.902 --> 00:19:51.097
Katie, somebody get that door!


00:19:52.239 --> 00:19:53.797
So...


00:19:54.675 --> 00:19:56.802
...that meeting today...


00:19:56.977 --> 00:19:59.775
...it was obvious
that your dad doesn't get you.


00:20:00.113 --> 00:20:02.172
He's an idiot for not liking your music.


00:20:02.349 --> 00:20:04.783
Well, it's... It's complicated.


00:20:05.052 --> 00:20:06.246
I'm gonna just, uh...


00:20:07.721 --> 00:20:09.621
Is it as complicated as me...


00:20:09.790 --> 00:20:12.918
...getting stuck outside
in only a welcome mat?


00:20:13.193 --> 00:20:16.924
That's not complicated.
That is a gift from God.


00:20:21.835 --> 00:20:24.633
Luke. Katie. What are you doing?


00:20:24.805 --> 00:20:27.865
Well, it seems your brother
is Satan's very own personal Mini-Me.


00:20:28.041 --> 00:20:30.305
Oh, I know, tell me about it. Come on in.


00:20:34.281 --> 00:20:35.942
Oh, my God, did you work out today?


00:20:37.617 --> 00:20:38.914
- Sit down.
- Ooh, look at this.


00:20:39.086 --> 00:20:42.180
- Ha, ha. Some lemonade.
- Why, thank you.


00:20:42.355 --> 00:20:44.823
You know, my stepsister,
she has body issues...


00:20:44.991 --> 00:20:47.152
...so I don't like
to discourage her nudity.


00:20:47.327 --> 00:20:48.521
That's interesting.


00:20:48.695 --> 00:20:51.459
- She's absolutely lovely...
- Would you like an appetizer?


00:20:51.631 --> 00:20:52.859
<i>Oh, fromage.</i>


00:20:53.033 --> 00:20:54.660
I only have cheese.


00:20:57.838 --> 00:20:59.806
I just got off the phone
with Guy Morgan.


00:20:59.973 --> 00:21:01.873
Your phone.


00:21:04.911 --> 00:21:07.778
He just loved that little demo
you left him.


00:21:07.948 --> 00:21:09.506
I have underestimated you.


00:21:10.083 --> 00:21:11.914
It'd make me proud
if I cared about you.


00:21:12.085 --> 00:21:15.179
- I didn't lie about anything.
- Oh, but, chicken, you did.


00:21:15.355 --> 00:21:17.983
At least that's what Guy thinks,
now that I've clarified.


00:21:18.158 --> 00:21:22.356
I told him it was Bev's demo
and that you stole it from her.


00:21:22.529 --> 00:21:25.794
- But you can't do that. That's my song.
- It's Bev's song.


00:21:25.966 --> 00:21:29.402
And Guy can't wait to see her perform it
at the Showcase.


00:21:29.569 --> 00:21:32.697
If you try to contact him, I'll deny
everything and lock you in the basement.


00:21:32.873 --> 00:21:38.004
- She can't sing to save her life.
- No, but you can, can't you?


00:21:39.279 --> 00:21:41.440
Now, let's hear this amazing voice.


00:21:46.853 --> 00:21:51.483
<i>Like a malignant tumor
She's got no sense of humor</i>


00:21:51.658 --> 00:21:55.754
<i>Just like a swollen blister
It's best to just resist her</i>


00:21:55.929 --> 00:21:59.695
<i>She's not exactly a witch
She's just a terrible bi...</i>


00:22:00.167 --> 00:22:01.828
Well, your lyrics stink.


00:22:02.002 --> 00:22:04.163
But Guy's right, you've got chops.


00:22:07.407 --> 00:22:10.103
Do you know what other instruments
I'm good at?


00:22:10.677 --> 00:22:14.135
I have a feeling I could get in trouble
with a question like that.


00:22:14.581 --> 00:22:16.549
I like trouble.


00:22:18.084 --> 00:22:19.210
Hey, kids.


00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:23.956
- Good evening, Miss Van Ravensway.
- Sorry, I need you to go. Now.


00:22:24.124 --> 00:22:26.888
Family emergency. I need Bev
to help me pass a kidney stone.


00:22:27.060 --> 00:22:30.894
- So she had a lovely evening. Ta-ta.
- Are you trying to ruin my life?


00:22:31.198 --> 00:22:36.431
I have figured out a way for you
to wow Guy Morgan in the Showcase.


00:22:36.636 --> 00:22:39.104
- So you do think I've improved?
- Oh, no, honey.


00:22:39.372 --> 00:22:41.932
But my month of spiritual devotion
has taught me...


00:22:42.108 --> 00:22:44.076
...that God works in annoying ways.


00:22:44.244 --> 00:22:47.304
How am I to wow Guy Morgan
if I supposedly can't sing?


00:22:47.480 --> 00:22:50.540
You can't, but Katie can.


00:22:50.717 --> 00:22:53.413
- What?
- I know. Like I said, annoying.


00:22:53.587 --> 00:22:56.886
We'll record her voice
and you will lip synch.


00:22:57.057 --> 00:22:58.888
What if I don't want to?


00:22:59.993 --> 00:23:03.724
Don't you get snarky with me,
you ungrateful toad.


00:23:03.897 --> 00:23:05.956
- I saved your life.
- You didn't do anything.


00:23:06.132 --> 00:23:08.396
- My dad married you.
- Yeah, and then he died.


00:23:08.568 --> 00:23:12.129
I tried to put you in foster care,
but they was all fulled up on ugly.


00:23:12.305 --> 00:23:13.795
- Funny.
- I thought it was...


00:23:13.974 --> 00:23:15.441
...because you don't wanna look bad.


00:23:17.043 --> 00:23:19.170
Katie, if you don't sing...


00:23:19.346 --> 00:23:22.474
...I'm gonna find a way for that savings
your dad left to disappear.


00:23:22.883 --> 00:23:27.081
That means, you forget college,
moving out, you're stuck here with me.


00:23:27.254 --> 00:23:31.088
But, pumpkin, we're gonna have
so much fun growing old together.


00:23:31.258 --> 00:23:34.159
Why don't you just have her perform
if you like her so much?


00:23:34.327 --> 00:23:36.591
Because, honey, look at you.


00:23:36.763 --> 00:23:38.890
You are a star.


00:23:39.065 --> 00:23:43.263
That is what Guy Morgan needs.
You, the star.


00:23:43.436 --> 00:23:44.994
I'm a star.


00:23:45.171 --> 00:23:49.335
- A bright, gassy star.
- Yes, you are.


00:23:49.509 --> 00:23:51.909
And Guy Morgan is gonna
give you a swimming pool...


00:23:52.078 --> 00:23:54.046
...shaped just like Colin Farrell.


00:23:54.214 --> 00:23:55.772
Every part of him.


00:23:55.949 --> 00:23:59.476
Or, Bev, you could just see every part
of Colin Farrell on the Internet.


00:23:59.653 --> 00:24:02.417
And just leave me out of this.


00:24:03.690 --> 00:24:06.250
- Okay, so how do we do this?
- First rule of Lie Club...


00:24:06.426 --> 00:24:08.326
...is don't talk about Lie Club.


00:24:08.929 --> 00:24:10.829
Which includes you, Katie.


00:24:10.997 --> 00:24:13.693
As far as everyone knows,
you can't sing.


00:24:13.867 --> 00:24:15.926
And no more talking to Luke or Guy.


00:24:16.102 --> 00:24:17.467
Are we clear?


00:24:17.904 --> 00:24:19.098
Crystal.


00:24:21.041 --> 00:24:24.033
Yeah, Dad, we're about to meet
some fresh talent right now.


00:24:24.210 --> 00:24:28.203
Remember when you signed Jay-Z?
No, you passed on him, my bad.


00:24:28.381 --> 00:24:30.849
Um, this is like that,
except it's gonna be brilliant.


00:24:31.017 --> 00:24:32.348
Yeah. Okay.


00:24:32.519 --> 00:24:34.646
- Yeah, okay. Bye.
- Dude, what'd he say?


00:24:34.821 --> 00:24:36.345
These guys you told me about are good?


00:24:36.523 --> 00:24:39.890
Yes. The Oral Majority has potential.
They'll be here any second.


00:24:40.060 --> 00:24:42.756
Talking about potential,
how was your little date with Bev?


00:24:42.929 --> 00:24:45.193
- Her mom kicked me out.
- I told you. Bev is drama.


00:24:45.365 --> 00:24:46.923
Technically, it was Gail's drama.


00:24:47.100 --> 00:24:49.227
But Bev's interesting, man. She's...


00:24:49.402 --> 00:24:50.869
I'm worried she's bonkers.


00:24:51.037 --> 00:24:53.870
See, my last girlfriend, she was hot,
but absolutely mental.


00:24:54.040 --> 00:24:56.702
I need a girl who's not gonna be
shipped to the loony bin.


00:24:56.876 --> 00:24:58.639
Hang on, I'm gonna hit the facilities.


00:24:58.812 --> 00:25:00.507
Facilities. That's a new one.


00:25:00.947 --> 00:25:03.643
- Hey, man. Sorry we're late.
- Hey, what's good, y'all?


00:25:03.817 --> 00:25:06.547
Nobody talks to my boy
until he comes from the facilities.


00:25:06.720 --> 00:25:07.914
We're here to impress.


00:25:08.088 --> 00:25:10.352
- Clear, right?
- Got it.


00:25:14.194 --> 00:25:16.662
<i>When you're fighting just to keep it sane</i>


00:25:16.830 --> 00:25:19.094
<i>Throw your will
At the eye of the hurricane</i>


00:25:19.265 --> 00:25:21.460
<i>- Sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:21.634 --> 00:25:25.001
<i>- Help me sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:25.171 --> 00:25:27.696
<i>If you wanna find out who you are
Stop running</i>


00:25:27.874 --> 00:25:31.139
<i>In the end you'll figure out
It's all about nothing</i>


00:25:31.311 --> 00:25:36.613
<i>All night, it's gonna be all right
Hey, hey, hey, hey</i>


00:25:36.783 --> 00:25:43.518
<i>All right
Turn your dreams into your life</i>


00:25:44.724 --> 00:25:46.214
That's good.


00:25:53.266 --> 00:25:56.565
I'm clean. No one followed me.
And I got your intel.


00:25:57.404 --> 00:25:59.736
Oh, Katie, baby, your life sucks.


00:25:59.906 --> 00:26:01.806
Trust me, it gets worse.


00:26:02.842 --> 00:26:06.437
Okay, dude, those guys, they
just went Oral Majority on me in there...


00:26:06.613 --> 00:26:08.808
- I was trying to hold them back...
- You're right.


00:26:08.982 --> 00:26:10.916
They have potential and they're great.


00:26:11.084 --> 00:26:16.317
But first, my talent-finding friend,
promise me no more auditions in the bogs.


00:26:16.489 --> 00:26:18.684
- The what?
- The loo.


00:26:19.225 --> 00:26:20.988
- Bathroom. Toilet.
- Got it.


00:26:21.161 --> 00:26:23.755
All right. Okay, come on.
I wanna show you something.


00:26:24.364 --> 00:26:27.663
So now I have to rehearse in secret.


00:26:27.834 --> 00:26:29.301
Why not not rehearse?


00:26:29.469 --> 00:26:31.494
Make Bev sound bad. What do you care?


00:26:31.671 --> 00:26:34.663
No song, no savings account. No life.


00:26:36.843 --> 00:26:39.277
People. Coming. Now.


00:26:42.816 --> 00:26:44.647
Okay.


00:26:45.218 --> 00:26:47.584
Dude, what are we doing?
The suspense is killing me.


00:26:47.921 --> 00:26:49.684
Can you grab the mike?


00:26:49.856 --> 00:26:51.847
Not about to serenade
a brother, are you?


00:26:52.025 --> 00:26:53.856
Dude, with bromance, comes a fine line.


00:26:54.027 --> 00:26:56.325
That I shall not cross.


00:26:56.796 --> 00:26:59.094
So sing something.


00:27:00.767 --> 00:27:02.234
Okay.


00:27:06.372 --> 00:27:09.170
<i>I'm lost in a world
That rattles my brain</i>


00:27:09.342 --> 00:27:11.833
<i>I'm cleaning up my life
From the mess you made</i>


00:27:12.011 --> 00:27:13.410
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:13.880 --> 00:27:15.871
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:17.684 --> 00:27:20.152
<i>My soul's in debt, but my bills are paid</i>


00:27:20.320 --> 00:27:22.845
<i>I'd give anything just to make an escape</i>


00:27:23.022 --> 00:27:24.614
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:25.125 --> 00:27:26.752
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:27.760 --> 00:27:30.695
<i>So you can keep
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:30.864 --> 00:27:33.196
<i>Baby, you're rockin'
But there ain't no way I'm ever letting you in</i>


00:27:33.366 --> 00:27:34.833
<i>He's amazing.</i>


00:27:36.236 --> 00:27:37.897
<i>Not again</i>


00:27:38.838 --> 00:27:41.671
<i>So keep on
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:41.841 --> 00:27:47.040
<i>But, baby, you're better off walking
'Cause I ain't gonna let you in</i>


00:27:47.213 --> 00:27:48.771
<i>Never again</i>


00:27:49.883 --> 00:27:52.477
<i>I went out on a limb again</i>


00:27:52.652 --> 00:27:55.212
<i>I guess I had to lose to win</i>


00:27:55.388 --> 00:27:59.757
<i>I was too confused to know
Which way to turn</i>


00:28:01.161 --> 00:28:03.823
<i>- And she could be a millionaire...
- Crap.</i>


00:28:03.997 --> 00:28:06.261
<i>- Gail needs me to drive her home.
- I don't care</i>


00:28:06.432 --> 00:28:09.094
<i>'Cause, baby, there's nobody home</i>


00:28:09.269 --> 00:28:11.760
<i>Nobody's home at all, yeah</i>


00:28:16.242 --> 00:28:18.369
- What? Did you write that?
- Yeah.


00:28:18.545 --> 00:28:21.173
Reminds me of, um... Uh...


00:28:21.347 --> 00:28:24.680
- Danger Fruit, right? Danger Fruit.
- Ha, ha. Because I wrote their album too.


00:28:24.951 --> 00:28:27.442
Shut up. Took me forever
to find that bootleg online.


00:28:27.620 --> 00:28:29.611
- I love that album. That's crazy.
- Yeah.


00:28:29.789 --> 00:28:32.087
My dad doesn't know.
And he thought the record...


00:28:32.258 --> 00:28:33.953
...was a pile of crap.


00:28:34.227 --> 00:28:35.922
He thinks writing's a waste of time.


00:28:36.362 --> 00:28:40.196
Because he basically wants me
to be like him. Only with better hair.


00:28:40.667 --> 00:28:44.763
But the first thing I thought when
I heard those guys in the urinals was...


00:28:44.938 --> 00:28:45.962
...good acoustics.


00:28:46.372 --> 00:28:50.206
Second thought was these guys,
these guys could be great.


00:28:50.376 --> 00:28:51.968
If you gave them your song.


00:28:53.379 --> 00:28:55.040
Mate, that's a brilliant idea.


00:28:55.782 --> 00:28:58.478
- So put them in the Showcase?
- Put them in the Showcase.


00:28:58.651 --> 00:28:59.982
Yeah.


00:29:01.654 --> 00:29:08.184
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:29:08.494 --> 00:29:09.791
You wrote that song today?


00:29:09.963 --> 00:29:13.421
- You've been home for what, two hours?
- It's like an answer to his song.


00:29:13.700 --> 00:29:14.997
You really like this guy.


00:29:15.168 --> 00:29:16.863
Yeah, I'm an idiot.


00:29:17.036 --> 00:29:19.231
You have to sing that for him.


00:29:19.405 --> 00:29:22.897
What if you sang to him in secret?


00:29:24.711 --> 00:29:27.509
At the dance. Ta-da.


00:29:31.117 --> 00:29:33.950
Okay, I know the card's
like, really cheesy, but...


00:29:35.989 --> 00:29:38.457
Oh, God, I hope you like it.


00:29:38.791 --> 00:29:42.283
Ange, it's beautiful,
but are you crazy?


00:29:42.462 --> 00:29:44.487
No, I know you're crazy.


00:29:44.664 --> 00:29:45.688
Am not.


00:29:46.733 --> 00:29:49.725
- What if he doesn't even like me?
- You'll both be in disguise.


00:29:49.902 --> 00:29:52.598
It's your chance to see
if he was really flirting with you.


00:29:52.772 --> 00:29:55.332
I was naked. Of course he was flirting.


00:29:55.508 --> 00:29:58.204
And why even torture myself?
It's not like I can have him.


00:29:58.378 --> 00:30:00.312
Why not? Tell him how you feel.


00:30:00.480 --> 00:30:04.507
If he feels the same way, you can reveal
your hot self and he won't tell Gail.


00:30:04.884 --> 00:30:07.978
And if he hates the song,
leave the disguise on.


00:30:10.923 --> 00:30:12.447
Okay.


00:30:12.759 --> 00:30:14.351
I'm going to the dance.


00:30:14.527 --> 00:30:15.858
That's my girl.


00:30:16.129 --> 00:30:20.122
<i>Maurice, no, no.
Again, in Français, longer legs.</i>


00:30:20.300 --> 00:30:23.599
I wouldn't go in your closet
for a little while if I were you.


00:30:23.770 --> 00:30:25.533
What? Why?


00:30:25.705 --> 00:30:27.070
Hey. Wake up.


00:30:30.977 --> 00:30:32.535
Katie!


00:30:32.712 --> 00:30:36.148
The cat has pooped in my closet.
I need you to clean it up.


00:30:36.316 --> 00:30:37.806
Go.


00:30:37.984 --> 00:30:39.713
I told you we don't have a cat.


00:30:39.886 --> 00:30:41.217
Angie, heads up.


00:30:43.189 --> 00:30:44.486
Katie!


00:30:49.696 --> 00:30:51.425
What's going on?


00:30:51.597 --> 00:30:53.030
Nothing.


00:30:53.199 --> 00:30:56.327
I am, uh, re-organizing and labeling. I...


00:30:56.502 --> 00:30:58.800
I took up crochet.
Do you want new socks?


00:30:58.971 --> 00:31:03.032
I would make you a sweater, but I hear
that the arms, that they're really hard.


00:31:06.279 --> 00:31:10.443
Oh, you thought you could sneak off
and go to the dance.


00:31:10.616 --> 00:31:12.846
After what you pulled today with Guy.


00:31:13.019 --> 00:31:14.452
Oh, no, no.


00:31:14.620 --> 00:31:17.111
Oh, no, no, no.


00:31:17.290 --> 00:31:19.588
You're on Victor watch tonight...


00:31:19.759 --> 00:31:22.455
...tomorrow night and every night.


00:31:22.628 --> 00:31:23.652
Fun.


00:31:23.830 --> 00:31:26.958
I'll give Victor all the mothering
you don't have time for.


00:31:27.133 --> 00:31:30.534
Oh, I wish you could be my mommy.


00:31:31.404 --> 00:31:33.429
I'm off to my cinnamon colonic.


00:31:37.410 --> 00:31:39.776
Hey. Get down.
You're gonna break yourself.


00:31:40.113 --> 00:31:42.377
Or worse, the furniture.


00:31:42.682 --> 00:31:45.776
Hello?
- Hey.


00:31:46.052 --> 00:31:49.215
- You look like you're having fun.
- Always.


00:31:49.555 --> 00:31:52.615
Well, I couldn't let you not go to the dance
without me.


00:31:52.792 --> 00:31:55.192
Besides, we have six hours
of shirtless Team Jacob.


00:31:55.361 --> 00:31:58.296
So let's just get this party started.


00:31:58.464 --> 00:32:02.491
- So is Victor driving you nuts?
- I swear to you, he's not human.


00:32:02.769 --> 00:32:06.068
I mean, can you really blame him, though?
Just look at this family.


00:32:07.273 --> 00:32:08.570
Victor, what are you doing?


00:32:18.551 --> 00:32:20.815
Oh, no. Great.


00:32:20.987 --> 00:32:23.182
Eh, she actually looks prettier
that way.


00:32:23.790 --> 00:32:26.816
True. Ugh. Whatever.


00:32:27.994 --> 00:32:31.122
Why did I ever think that tonight
could've been something special.


00:32:31.898 --> 00:32:34.162
Think Bev's all over Luke at the dance
right now?


00:32:34.333 --> 00:32:36.631
They're probably making out. See?


00:32:36.803 --> 00:32:40.000
- Victor, give it a rest.
- Just check it out. Come on.


00:32:43.209 --> 00:32:45.837
<i>Luke is gonna produce
whoever wins the Showcase.</i>


00:32:46.012 --> 00:32:49.072
<i>So we need a little insurance.</i>


00:32:49.248 --> 00:32:52.445
<i>- I know what I'm doing, Mother.
Do you?</i>


00:32:53.352 --> 00:32:56.219
I can't take it anymore, okay?


00:32:56.389 --> 00:32:58.448
I'm taking my life into my own hands.


00:32:58.624 --> 00:32:59.716
I'm talking to Luke.


00:33:00.326 --> 00:33:02.817
- Finally.
- Okay, but we have gotta be home...


00:33:02.995 --> 00:33:04.462
...before Gail gets here.


00:33:05.198 --> 00:33:06.529
What about the demon spawn?


00:33:06.699 --> 00:33:07.723
Mm-hm.


00:33:07.900 --> 00:33:09.299
Right.


00:33:10.303 --> 00:33:11.702
Okay, just watch him.


00:33:14.774 --> 00:33:16.036
Hmm.


00:33:20.847 --> 00:33:22.838
Is that all you've got, Angela?


00:33:23.516 --> 00:33:24.540
Ravi?


00:33:26.219 --> 00:33:28.744
My sister could catch that, jerknut.


00:33:28.921 --> 00:33:31.355
Put some nuts in that sack, ref.


00:33:33.493 --> 00:33:36.053
Miss Katie, I am most startled.


00:33:36.229 --> 00:33:37.423
Obviously.


00:33:37.964 --> 00:33:40.455
All right. All right. Don't hate me.


00:33:40.633 --> 00:33:42.191
Okay, don't hate me. I'm sorry.


00:33:42.368 --> 00:33:45.735
But my name ain't Ravi. It's Tony.


00:33:46.272 --> 00:33:49.400
- Tony.
- Tony Gupta from Jersey.


00:33:49.575 --> 00:33:52.237
- From Jersey.
- I am half Indian.


00:33:52.612 --> 00:33:56.013
My friends call me Meatball
because I'm half Italian.


00:33:56.182 --> 00:33:58.047
Truth is I always wanted to be an actor.


00:33:58.417 --> 00:33:59.941
But I never got my shot.


00:34:00.119 --> 00:34:02.349
I'm working at KFC,
and one day, Gail comes in...


00:34:02.522 --> 00:34:04.922
...she's like, "Are you Indian?"
I'm like, "What?"


00:34:05.091 --> 00:34:07.286
She's like, "Are you a guru?"
I'm like:


00:34:07.460 --> 00:34:08.950
"Who is asking?"


00:34:09.228 --> 00:34:12.595
She says, "Someone
who's paying for some spiritual guidance."


00:34:12.765 --> 00:34:15.359
And I'm like, "Whaa! It's a miracle!"


00:34:15.535 --> 00:34:19.904
I finally get a chance to do
a total immersion into a character.


00:34:20.206 --> 00:34:22.470
Real training and I get paid.
Are you kidding me?


00:34:22.642 --> 00:34:25.042
Ravi is my King Lear.


00:34:25.378 --> 00:34:28.006
<i>You wanna hear
the monologue from My Fair Lady?</i>


00:34:28.180 --> 00:34:29.374
- Oy, mate.
- No, thanks.


00:34:30.583 --> 00:34:33.279
I'm sorry I barged in. Whoops.


00:34:36.088 --> 00:34:39.751
Your secret's safe with me, okay?
But I need to ask you a favor.


00:34:40.426 --> 00:34:42.485
- Meatball.
- Ha, Meatball.


00:34:42.662 --> 00:34:45.130
Please watch Victor tonight
so I can go to the dance?


00:34:45.298 --> 00:34:46.356
Are you kidding me? Done.


00:34:47.934 --> 00:34:49.265
Blow it up.


00:34:51.203 --> 00:34:52.761
Thank you.


00:35:02.582 --> 00:35:03.981
Whoa.


00:35:04.150 --> 00:35:06.778
How am I supposed to find Luke
if everybody's got a mask?


00:35:06.953 --> 00:35:10.013
I never said this was
gonna be easy. Let's do some recon.


00:35:11.390 --> 00:35:13.722
I am Assistant Principal
Dorothy Plumberg.


00:35:13.893 --> 00:35:17.124
No drinking. No texting. No kissing.


00:35:19.832 --> 00:35:22.801
Luke? No. Luke Morgan?


00:35:22.969 --> 00:35:26.598
No leaving the premises
and no experiencing joy of any kind.


00:35:27.306 --> 00:35:29.638
Luke? Ugh.


00:35:35.014 --> 00:35:36.447
Where is he?


00:35:37.283 --> 00:35:40.081
That reminds me.
I got a new act for you to listen to.


00:35:40.252 --> 00:35:41.913
- Now?
- No time like it.


00:35:42.088 --> 00:35:44.522
- Dude, not again...
- We're called Big Pain Ticket.


00:35:48.027 --> 00:35:51.588
<i>I wanna kiss your apocalypse</i>


00:35:51.764 --> 00:35:55.097
<i>Wrap you in my Armageddon</i>


00:35:55.267 --> 00:35:57.462
<i>Sing you a twisted serenade</i>


00:35:57.670 --> 00:36:00.400
They're good, but I'm worried
that chain saw's unsafe.


00:36:00.573 --> 00:36:03.007
Dude, the chain saw's,
like, the best part.


00:36:09.815 --> 00:36:10.873
I think I found him.


00:36:11.050 --> 00:36:13.314
Well, he is blond.


00:36:16.422 --> 00:36:18.720
Oh, my God, what is she doing here?


00:36:20.626 --> 00:36:22.924
I hate teenage desperation.


00:36:23.095 --> 00:36:24.494
What are you doing here?


00:36:24.664 --> 00:36:27.497
Oh, honey, the prize pig
doesn't win the blue ribbon...


00:36:27.667 --> 00:36:29.692
...by covering up its third best asset.


00:36:29.869 --> 00:36:32.804
A, what does that even mean
and, B, did you just call me a pig?


00:36:32.972 --> 00:36:34.803
Honey, I saw you making sweet love...


00:36:34.974 --> 00:36:37.442
...to a plate of Swedish meatballs
at the snack table.


00:36:39.879 --> 00:36:42.006
It's now or never, babe.


00:36:43.549 --> 00:36:46.985
- What if she recognizes me?
- I'll distract her. Go.


00:36:47.153 --> 00:36:49.348
- So was I right or was I right?
- You were right.


00:36:49.522 --> 00:36:52.389
You have very cool taste.
Any more auditions in the men's...


00:36:52.558 --> 00:36:54.492
...and you're fired.


00:36:57.530 --> 00:37:01.057
- I know your secret.
- Which secret is that?


00:37:03.669 --> 00:37:05.159
I heard you sing at school.


00:37:05.404 --> 00:37:06.530
You were amazing.


00:37:06.706 --> 00:37:07.764
Do I know you?


00:37:12.111 --> 00:37:14.705
- I wanna show you something.
- What's your name?


00:37:17.049 --> 00:37:19.108
Angela, what are you doing?


00:37:19.752 --> 00:37:22.243
I'd like to make a request.


00:37:26.759 --> 00:37:29.592
I will make your night. I promise.


00:37:29.762 --> 00:37:31.127
Miss Van R.


00:37:31.764 --> 00:37:34.164
Is it true you wanted to be a dancer
when you were younger...


00:37:34.333 --> 00:37:35.527
...but were never good enough?


00:37:36.902 --> 00:37:38.563
Who told you that?


00:37:56.288 --> 00:37:57.721
Well, now, how lovely.


00:37:57.890 --> 00:38:01.087
But I've seen better dancing
in a Filipino prison, sugar.


00:38:01.260 --> 00:38:02.386
Oh!


00:38:02.561 --> 00:38:06.793
Really? Because I think
I just challenged you to a dance battle.


00:38:11.137 --> 00:38:14.231
Would Luke Morgan please pick up
the white courtesy phone?


00:38:14.406 --> 00:38:17.307
Luke Morgan, white courtesy phone.


00:38:22.081 --> 00:38:24.811
Hold on. What is that?
You've never seen a guitar before?


00:38:25.151 --> 00:38:27.847
You hid a guitar in there.
You hiding anything else?


00:38:28.020 --> 00:38:29.282
Follow me.


00:38:34.326 --> 00:38:36.157
Oh, wow.


00:38:38.631 --> 00:38:44.194
Madam, while your exquisite eyes
tell of a radiant, but mischievous beauty...


00:38:45.070 --> 00:38:46.970
...I have grown impatient.


00:38:47.139 --> 00:38:50.836
Off with your veil,
so that I may know the truth.


00:38:52.344 --> 00:38:53.538
Or not.


00:38:55.815 --> 00:38:58.841
I'm hoping this answers
a lot of your questions.


00:39:05.057 --> 00:39:08.618
<i>I can see it from the spark in your eyes</i>


00:39:09.929 --> 00:39:14.161
<i>You believe in all the things
You've denied</i>


00:39:14.333 --> 00:39:17.860
<i>You wanna fly
And leave your worries behind</i>


00:39:18.037 --> 00:39:22.030
<i>Don't you? Don't you?</i>


00:39:24.009 --> 00:39:27.342
<i>Well, now I'm knocking
At your front door</i>


00:39:29.114 --> 00:39:32.811
<i>And I'm looking for the right cure</i>


00:39:33.485 --> 00:39:37.182
<i>I'm still a little bit unsure</i>


00:39:37.656 --> 00:39:40.489
Okay, now take off that veil.


00:39:40.960 --> 00:39:42.052
Uh-uh.


00:42:20.986 --> 00:42:23.580
I think I've blown something.


00:42:23.756 --> 00:42:26.816
Does anyone else smell cinnamon?


00:42:29.428 --> 00:42:30.986
Move it, fatso.


00:42:32.731 --> 00:42:39.330
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:42:40.072 --> 00:42:43.701
Okay, you are blowing my mind.
You have to show me who you are.


00:42:56.255 --> 00:42:57.688
- We have to go.
- What?


00:42:57.856 --> 00:42:59.881
- Come.
- No, Ange.


00:43:00.059 --> 00:43:02.619
In the middle of a really big moment
right now.


00:43:02.795 --> 00:43:04.763
Someone had an accident
and went home.


00:43:07.232 --> 00:43:08.597
I'm so sorry.


00:43:09.301 --> 00:43:10.529
What...? You...?


00:43:11.236 --> 00:43:12.897
Hey. Wait.


00:43:13.072 --> 00:43:14.300
But who are you?


00:43:14.473 --> 00:43:17.067
Over here. Go, go, go.


00:43:25.217 --> 00:43:28.243
- We beat her.
- I love you for this.


00:43:46.705 --> 00:43:48.730
Interesting babysitting attire.


00:43:49.508 --> 00:43:52.443
I should've known
you'd go behind my back again.


00:43:52.878 --> 00:43:55.813
And that Paula Abdul wannabe,
trying to distract me.


00:43:56.148 --> 00:43:58.343
Don't talk about her like that.


00:44:00.352 --> 00:44:03.515
Your friend wants to be a choreographer,
if memory serves.


00:44:03.689 --> 00:44:07.250
She might've made a decent one
if she hadn't gotten herself expelled.


00:44:07.426 --> 00:44:09.690
Guess she can kiss
them Juilliard dreams goodbye.


00:44:09.862 --> 00:44:12.922
Look, I'll do whatever you want.
Okay? Just leave Ange out of this.


00:44:13.232 --> 00:44:16.360
That depends if you pull another stunt
like tonight, sugar.


00:44:17.269 --> 00:44:20.397
- I won't.
- I'll be taking this.


00:44:26.912 --> 00:44:30.143
Only her eyes were piercing out
through this veil, but her voice...


00:44:30.315 --> 00:44:32.374
How hot was the girl
on a scale of one to 10?


00:44:32.551 --> 00:44:34.485
- An 11.
- The hotness scale only goes 10.


00:44:34.653 --> 00:44:36.348
Yeah, this girl has love potential.


00:44:36.522 --> 00:44:38.820
- Ooh, love.
- Shut it.


00:44:40.192 --> 00:44:44.322
We are gonna do this for hours
until we get it right. Even if it takes hours.


00:44:45.297 --> 00:44:48.892
Now, sing like your life depends on it.
Because, sugar, it does.


00:44:49.968 --> 00:44:51.595
We're recording.


00:44:51.904 --> 00:44:53.735
<i>Plug in the mike</i>


00:44:53.906 --> 00:44:55.134
<i>Open the curtain</i>


00:44:55.741 --> 00:44:57.675
<i>Turn on the lights</i>


00:44:57.843 --> 00:44:59.572
<i>I'm through rehearsing</i>


00:44:59.745 --> 00:45:02.077
- Dang, she's good, man.
- Told you, man.


00:45:02.247 --> 00:45:03.475
Check this out, all right?


00:45:03.649 --> 00:45:07.244
Thirty-nine girls in the singing program
which means 85 percent...


00:45:07.419 --> 00:45:09.250
...have music during the sixth period.


00:45:09.421 --> 00:45:11.252
So your girl's in one of those rooms.


00:45:11.456 --> 00:45:13.481
<i>The feeling ignites</i>


00:45:13.659 --> 00:45:14.819
<i>I'm in control</i>


00:45:14.993 --> 00:45:16.961
Oh, cut. Cut.


00:45:17.129 --> 00:45:18.994
That was subpar at best.


00:45:19.164 --> 00:45:21.689
From the top, pretty please.


00:45:22.434 --> 00:45:25.733
<i>Amazing grace</i>


00:45:25.904 --> 00:45:27.462
It's cool, I got this.


00:45:27.639 --> 00:45:30.005
Ladies, all my single ladies.


00:45:30.175 --> 00:45:33.201
My boy Luke here has a special favor
to ask of you, all right?


00:45:33.378 --> 00:45:36.472
He needs vocals
for this big show coming up, so...


00:45:36.648 --> 00:45:38.206
- My name is...
- Luke Morgan.


00:45:38.650 --> 00:45:41.517
You will put me in the Showcase.
Oh, yes, you will.


00:45:42.054 --> 00:45:45.615
- Maybe I could ask you to sing first?
- I am so gonna rock your world.


00:45:45.891 --> 00:45:49.224
<i>I love the way you love me, Luke</i>


00:45:49.394 --> 00:45:51.988
<i>Inside my head every night</i>


00:45:52.164 --> 00:45:54.632
<i>You come and kiss me good night</i>


00:45:54.800 --> 00:45:57.894
<i>Whatever you see is what you get</i>


00:45:58.070 --> 00:46:00.595
Why don't you not suck
and do it again, okay?


00:46:02.341 --> 00:46:06.937
<i>I wanna be with you forever...</i>


00:46:07.112 --> 00:46:10.081
What is going on in here? Disgusting.


00:46:10.249 --> 00:46:13.082
You two boys are not in my class.
Stop. Wait.


00:46:19.124 --> 00:46:22.321
Stop. Wait. Stop.


00:46:41.446 --> 00:46:43.744
<i>I got nothing to lose</i>


00:46:43.915 --> 00:46:45.109
<i>I've been exposed</i>


00:46:45.284 --> 00:46:47.582
<i>I'm paying my dues</i>


00:46:47.753 --> 00:46:49.118
<i>Playing the role</i>


00:46:49.955 --> 00:46:52.082
- Oh, really?
- We are back where we started.


00:46:52.257 --> 00:46:53.383
This is not good.


00:46:54.960 --> 00:46:56.757
That's her. That's her voice.


00:46:56.928 --> 00:46:58.759
Don't think you can get away from me.


00:46:58.930 --> 00:47:01.330
- Step aside. Step aside.
- Please. Wait.


00:47:01.500 --> 00:47:04.936
Okay. But first, why don't you
just both audition for me.


00:47:05.103 --> 00:47:06.127
Listen...


00:47:06.305 --> 00:47:09.741
<i>Luke, you are the one for me, yes you are</i>


00:47:09.908 --> 00:47:11.569
<i>You just don't know it yet</i>


00:47:23.422 --> 00:47:27.415
<i>Make you believe in me</i>


00:47:27.592 --> 00:47:30.584
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:30.762 --> 00:47:34.391
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:34.566 --> 00:47:38.502
<i>That I can be
Anything, anything, anything</i>


00:47:38.670 --> 00:47:42.470
<i>I'll make you believe in me</i>


00:47:43.008 --> 00:47:45.909
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:46.078 --> 00:47:49.138
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:50.949 --> 00:47:52.883
It was you?


00:47:53.552 --> 00:47:56.646
- Oh, sorry to interrupt.
- Oh, no, honey. Interrupt away.


00:47:57.589 --> 00:48:01.423
I didn't think I'd see you. It was killing me.
Because I felt like we connected.


00:48:03.061 --> 00:48:06.087
Excuse me.
Uh, how exactly did you two connect?


00:48:06.264 --> 00:48:09.028
Yeah, how did we? I mean, we did.


00:48:09.201 --> 00:48:11.328
- Through...
- With your lyrics. They just...


00:48:11.970 --> 00:48:14.700
- I can't get them out of my head.
- My lyrics. Yeah.


00:48:14.973 --> 00:48:16.736
Well, how wonderful.


00:48:16.908 --> 00:48:20.275
But, uh, Bev has to prepare
for her Showcase audition.


00:48:20.445 --> 00:48:22.709
Oh, no. She doesn't need to audition.
You're in.


00:48:24.216 --> 00:48:26.013
Do you wanna grab a bite later?


00:48:26.184 --> 00:48:27.276
- Yeah.
Wait.


00:48:28.220 --> 00:48:29.687
You have a date with detention.


00:48:29.855 --> 00:48:31.322
Actually, he has a date with me.


00:48:31.490 --> 00:48:33.219
Dear me, did I not fire you?


00:48:33.392 --> 00:48:36.088
- I have tenure.
- One call and you're wearing a paper hat...


00:48:36.261 --> 00:48:39.389
...that says "Welcome to McDonald's.
How may I take your order?"


00:48:39.564 --> 00:48:41.054
- Five calls.
- Two calls and text.


00:48:41.233 --> 00:48:43.133
Two calls, a text, several long e-mails.


00:48:43.301 --> 00:48:46.099
One text and a Tweet.
- One text and a re-Tweet.


00:48:46.271 --> 00:48:48.637
Oh, for God's sakes,
go lick a chalkboard.


00:48:48.807 --> 00:48:50.274
Fine.


00:48:51.076 --> 00:48:52.600
I hate you.


00:48:56.248 --> 00:49:00.378
Okay. Um, I'd love to write a song with you.
Let's talk about it tonight?


00:49:00.652 --> 00:49:02.586
- I'd love to.
- Okay, you're on.


00:49:09.161 --> 00:49:10.788
I've always wanted to write a song.


00:49:10.962 --> 00:49:14.159
Maybe I'll write about my skin.
They say love tightens your pores.


00:49:14.332 --> 00:49:15.799
What rhymes with pores?


00:49:15.967 --> 00:49:18.765
Chores. Bores. Sores.


00:49:18.937 --> 00:49:21.132
Katie, I've got a new task for you.


